	skos:definition	"""Providers of consumer finance services, including personal credit, credit cards, lease financing, travel-related money services and pawn shops.

This Sub-Industry includes companies that purchase debt portfolios at a discount from other companies and engage in collection from debtors and earn interest on the debts. It also includes lending facilitation companies operating peer to peer (P2P) Internet communities where users borrow and lend money online.

This Sub-Industry excludes mortgage lenders classified in the Commercial & Residential Mortgage Finance Sub-Industry."""@en ;
	skos:notation	"40202010" ;
	tempo:validFrom	"2003-05-01"^^xsd:date .

